Scheduled Apex — the concept, in four lines
apex
public class NightlyTierJob implements Schedulable {
    public void execute(SchedulableContext sc) {
        Database.executeBatch(new TierRecalculationBatch(), 200);
    }
}

That's the whole thing. One interface, one method. It doesn't do work — it starts work at a time. Almost every real Schedulable is three lines that kick off a batch.

Scheduling it:

apex
System.schedule('Nightly Tier Recalc', '0 0 2 * * ?', new NightlyTierJob());

That cron string is 2am daily. You'll look up cron syntax every single time — nobody memorizes it.

Same shape as everything this week: implement an interface, Salesforce calls your execute. Fourth time in five days.

